{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Who</b> — The prophet addresses every prince and king: if you are considered in your own eyes like a great mountain, [you will become] a plain. You shall turn before Zerubbabel, and when he brings out the chief stone — it is the tin stone that shall be placed in Zerubbabel's hand, and it is the one mentioned above, which I set before Joshua." "<b>Shouts</b> — There shall be a great noise for it: 'Grace, grace to it' — everyone shall rejoice, as in 'full of shouts' [1 Samuel 4:5]."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:45:55.604277566Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}